A||||6||dlancer407||Rust in my rear end||||1||
Z||000000||dlancer407||08-17-2001||08:05 PM||||Hi All; I know rust has been covered here before. My question is has anyone had a serious structural problem due to rust in the rear end of there Fiero. My car has rust in the trunk area and around the inner wheel wells in the back. I know from past posts that this a common problem on Fiero's. Is it good enough to patch the holes I can see and do a good undercoating on the area. Has any one had any problems with the frame itself rusting out.Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||AkursedX||08-17-2001||09:07 PM||||I am going through the same type of situation in my other GT.  A friend of mine who is a welder is taking some thick plate and welding it along the main frame rails to reinforce the part that rusted through.  Then he is just using some thinner plate to patch up the holes in the trunk.  <P>If you know someone who can weld some reinforcement in, then I would suggest you do that.  If not, then make sure to sandblast all the rust away, and you might want to use some rust converter and spray it over with that, then paint it and undercoat it.  <P>I think that the frame rail and the strut towers are probably the 2 most important places to keep rust free, and if those are rusted through, then I think you would have some serious problems.  <P>When I'm all done with my welding, sandblasting, painting, and undercoating, I plan on posting some before and after pictures, but that probably won't be for another couple weeks.  <P>Hope this helps a little<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||85 gt fiero||08-17-2001||09:12 PM||||if you're talking about the wheel well by the battery sometimes your battery will leak acid and start to corrode the metal and undercarriage. Yes i have heard of peoples fieros rusting out and since the body is fiberglass the water will run to the back cradles and start to rust them. You might be good if you could go to a salvage yard and have them take off a good engine cradle about 100 for that. Thats only if your engine cradle is bad. You can take it to frame shops and have them weld extra beam supports.  Hope you get it fixed.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||11-07-2001||04:24 PM||||what would be a general estimate of cost for having a body shop/welding shop patch some (big) holes in the trunk & rear wheel wells, and replacing about 12" of the rear frame by the battery tray?<P>(battery is going to be moved to the front compartment, not gonna bother fabricating a new tray)<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||11-28-2001||09:21 PM||||ok, update.. rust damage is worse than I thought, the whole back end needs replacing. they quoted me $800...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||11-28-2001||09:30 PM||||Rust?  What is this word, rust?  I don't believe I have ever seen rust.....can somone enlighten me?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry to tease you, but I just love living in a rust free area! <P>What exactly is rusted out on your Fiero that costs $800 to patch up?  <P>I have seen some crusty engine cradles, but that is easy enough to fix.....just swap out cradles.  You can do that with the engine and tranny still in place (just get one of those support things).  If it's the actual frame rails that are bad then I would suggest buying another (rust free) Fiero chassis and swapping your goodies over.<P>I wish you luck.....there is nothing worse than a rusty car.<P><BR>I just re-read your post.<P>I think $800 (even if it is Canadian  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) is too much to pay for the repairs you mentioned.  Shop it around or do it yourself in the springtime when the weather is nice.<P>You may have to remove the rear clip to get at the frame rail which might account for some of that $800 quote.<P>Good luck. <P><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000006||jelly2m8||11-28-2001||10:38 PM||||Heres some rusty fiero pics. These pics do the car justice, it is even worse than it looks.<P> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/P8120019.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/P8120020.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/P8120022.jpg"> <P> BTW I do rear frame rebuilds on Fieros, and prices for the final result is generally 1500-1800 canadian.<P>Thats start to finish, r&r clip and all associated parts, do rebuild, all materials, all seams sealed, primed and repainted.<P> 800 canadian is not a bad  price, it is a very involved procedure. I usually tell customers to expect the car to be in repair over a 2 week period. This includes complete upper frame rail replacement also.<P> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
